<script lang="ts">
	import Demo from "./demo.svelte";
</script>

# Code Block

Displays highlighted code with Shiki, and an optional header with a file label and a copy button. The theme follows the `.dark` class by default, or you can set it with `theme`.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { CodeBlock, CodeBlockCode, CodeBlockHeader } from "#lib/components/ui/code-block/index.js";

	const code = `export const add = (a: number, b: number) => a + b;`;
</script>

<CodeBlock data={{ code, path: "src/lib/math.ts" }}>
	<CodeBlockHeader />
	<CodeBlockCode />
</CodeBlock>
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/code-block.json
```

## Parts

`CodeBlock` is the root and shares its `data`, `theme`, and `size` with its children through context. `CodeBlockHeader` shows the label and copy button, and `CodeBlockCode` shows the highlighted code. Leave out the header to show code only.

## Language and title

Pass a `path` to detect the language from the file extension, or pass `lang` to set it directly. Supported languages are `typescript`, `svelte`, `json`, `css`, `bash`, and `markdown`. Unknown extensions fall back to `bash`. Add a `title` to replace the path in the header.

<Demo section="title" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<CodeBlock data={{ code, lang: "css", title: "Card styles" }}>
	<CodeBlockHeader />
	<CodeBlockCode />
</CodeBlock>
```

## Header label

The header uses `data.title` first, then its own `path` prop, then `data.path`. When none is set, the header is hidden.

<Demo section="header" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<CodeBlock data={{ code, lang: "bash" }}>
	<CodeBlockHeader />
	<CodeBlockCode />
</CodeBlock>

<CodeBlock data={{ code, lang: "bash" }}>
	<CodeBlockHeader path="Terminal" />
	<CodeBlockCode />
</CodeBlock>
```

## Line highlight

Set `highlightLines` to an array of line numbers, such as `[2, 4]`, or a range string, such as `"1,3-5"`. Lines start at `1`, and numbers past the last line are ignored. `CodeBlockCode` also accepts `highlightLines`, which overrides the code block's `highlightLines`. In `.svx` pages and `Svdown`, add the lines in braces after the language, such as `ts {1,3-5}`.

<Demo section="highlight" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<CodeBlock data={{ code, path: "src/lib/math.ts" }} highlightLines="1-2">
	<CodeBlockHeader />
	<CodeBlockCode />
</CodeBlock>

<CodeBlock data={{ code, lang: "css" }}>
	<CodeBlockHeader />
	<CodeBlockCode highlightLines={[2, 4]} />
</CodeBlock>
```

## Encoded data

Set `usingEncodedData` when `data.code` is UTF-8 Base64, such as code embedded by a build step. The code is decoded before display and copying, and malformed Base64 throws.

<Demo section="encoded" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { CodeBlock, CodeBlockCode, CodeBlockHeader, encodeAndDecodeString } from "#lib/components/ui/code-block/index.js";

	const code = encodeAndDecodeString(`console.log("Hello");`, "encode");
</script>

<CodeBlock data={{ code, path: "encoded.ts" }} usingEncodedData>
	<CodeBlockHeader />
	<CodeBlockCode />
</CodeBlock>
```

## Theme

`theme` defaults to `auto`, which renders both highlight themes and switches to dark when an ancestor has the `.dark` class. Set `theme` to `light` or `dark` to force one, such as when your app tracks dark mode in its own state. `CodeBlockCode` also accepts `theme`, which overrides the code block's `theme`.

<Demo section="theme" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<CodeBlock data={{ code, lang: "bash", title: "Light" }} theme="light">
	<CodeBlockHeader />
	<CodeBlockCode />
</CodeBlock>

<CodeBlock data={{ code, lang: "bash", title: "Dark" }} theme="dark">
	<CodeBlockHeader />
	<CodeBlockCode />
</CodeBlock>
```

## Sizes

Set `size` to `xs`, `sm`, `md`, or `lg` to change the header height, code padding, and font size. The default is `md`, and the corner radius follows the size.

<Demo section="sizes" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<CodeBlock data={{ code, lang: "bash" }} size="sm">
	<CodeBlockHeader />
	<CodeBlockCode />
</CodeBlock>
```

## Rounded

Set `rounded` to `xs` through `4xl` or `pill` to override the radius from the size. `pill` is a true pill and can clip tall content, so use `3xl` or `4xl` for round corners that stay safe.

<Demo section="rounded" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<CodeBlock data={{ code, lang: "bash" }} rounded="lg">
	<CodeBlockHeader />
	<CodeBlockCode />
</CodeBlock>
```

## API

`CodeBlock` extends the native `div` attributes. `CodeBlockHeader` extends the `header` attributes, and `CodeBlockCode` extends the `div` attributes. Each part merges `class` onto its element.

```ts title="index.ts"
type CodeBlockData = { code: string; lang: AvailableShikiLangs; title?: string } | { code: string; path: string; title?: string };

type CodeBlockTheme = "auto" | "light" | "dark";

type CodeBlockHighlightLines = number[] | string;

interface Props extends CompPropsWithChild<"div"> {
	/** Code and language metadata; `title` takes precedence over the header path label */
	data: CodeBlockData;
	/** Decodes `data.code` from UTF-8 Base64 before display and copying; malformed Base64 throws during decoding */
	usingEncodedData?: boolean;
	/** Highlight theme shared with the code; defaults to `auto`, which follows the `.dark` class on an ancestor */
	theme?: CodeBlockTheme;
	/** Lines to highlight, such as `[2, 4]` or `"1,3-5"`; shared with the code */
	highlightLines?: CodeBlockHighlightLines;
	/** Header height, code padding, and font size */
	size?: UiSize;
	/** Corner radius; follows `size` when omitted. `pill` is a true pill that can clip the content, so use `3xl` or `4xl` to stay round */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
}

interface HeaderProps extends CompProps<"header"> {
	/** Header label used after `data.title` and before `data.path`; a nonempty value also shows the header */
	path?: string;
}

interface CodeProps extends CompProps<"div"> {
	/** Highlight theme; overrides the code block's `theme` */
	theme?: CodeBlockTheme;
	/** Lines to highlight, such as `[2, 4]` or `"1,3-5"`; overrides the code block's `highlightLines` */
	highlightLines?: CodeBlockHighlightLines;
}
```
